WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.824
Teams model a building's structure,
ducts and pipes separately.

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.336
When the models come together, they clash.

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:11.015
Finding and fixing those
clashes takes engineers days.

00:00:11.314 --> 00:00:14.186
AI can help,
but it can be confidently wrong.

00:00:15.195 --> 00:00:16.283
Meet Iris.

00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:17.559
AI proposes.

00:00:17.796 --> 00:00:18.942
Geometry proves.

00:00:19.168 --> 00:00:20.276
The engineer decides.

00:00:21.285 --> 00:00:25.088
Northbank, the sample building,
has four models from different teams.

00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:29.879
Iris finds 464 clashes,
in about 11 seconds on the cloud.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:36.374
Clash #1: a supply-air duct runs right
through a transfer girder, one metre deep.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.259
They overlap by 300 mm.

00:00:39.344 --> 00:00:41.932
Iris shows it in 3D, with three pictures.

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:46.855
Prepare fixes.
Gemini proposes real edits to the model.

00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:51.374
Then geometry re-checks every one:
the clash is gone, the clearance met,

00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:52.593
and nothing new hit.

00:00:53.604 --> 00:00:55.509
All 8 fixes are verified.

00:00:56.013 --> 00:00:57.029
On the girder clashes,

00:00:57.029 --> 00:01:02.439
they match the designer's own revision:
up 400, 250 and 280 mm.

00:01:03.654 --> 00:01:06.253
Here it is before, and after the fix.

00:01:08.381 --> 00:01:11.085
Nothing changes
until the engineer accepts it.

00:01:12.095 --> 00:01:18.688
Then export the report: a PDF, and a BCF
file for Revit, Navisworks and Solibri.

00:01:19.952 --> 00:01:21.112
AI proposes.

00:01:21.112 --> 00:01:22.368
Geometry proves.

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:23.918
The engineer decides.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:27.156
Try it at iris-techjays.web.app.
